      <Comment source="AU4FS-4">Sesamin is a lignan characterized from sesame oil. It has been reported to inhibit |FRAME: MONOMER-12526| activity and hence the conversion of |FRAME: CPD-8120| to |FRAME: ARACHIDONIC_ACID|. Sesamin can also inhibit |FRAME: MONOMER-16595 &quot;Acyl-CoA:lysophosphatidylcholine acyltransferase&quot;| (LPCAT) activity in the filamentous fungus |FRAME: TAX-64518| |CITS: [11171183]|. LPCAT is responsible for the acylation of sn-1-acyl-lysophosphatidylcholine to yield phosphatidylcholine.</Comment>
